## Loop Architecture

**Phases 1–2 run ONCE per task. On resume: skip to Phase 3 at pending section.**

| Phase | What happens |
|---|---|
| 1 Info Gather | G1 scan all sections → G2 batch greps+reads → G3 assess · emit [✓ gather] |
| 2 MECE Plan | Plan + Verify-N → user confirms → roadmap → mece_plan.md |
| 3 Execution | REACT LOOP: Select → Execute → Observe → Verify → Decide |

> **Dynamic fan-out (run-time · anywhere · T-481):** parallelism is NOT limited to a pre-declared Phase-3 cycle. At ANY point where ≥2 independent units are queued, the Orchestrator may run a 4-check gate — (1) ≥2 independent units · (2) no shared WRITE target (reads always parallel-safe) · (3) each unit ≥ a size floor (~≥3 tool calls) · (4) latency worth it — and if all pass, spawn a parallel batch with a barrier, REUSING the §14d cycle machinery (no new schema). A shared-WRITE output routes through **map-reduce** (parallel draft into own files → one serial merge). Single source: **Implement/06_orchestrator.md §14f**.

